Wraps the ESPN core-v2 endpoint
\code{sports.core.api.espn.com/v2/sports/football/leagues/college-football/seasons/{year}/athletes/{athlete_id}}.
The season-scoped path is used so the returned \code{team_id} reflects the
team the player was on \emph{that} season. The wrapper returns a single-row
tibble: scalar bio fields are flattened inline, nested objects
(\code{position}, \code{status}, \code{birthPlace}, \code{experience}) are flattened with a
prefix, and the nested \verb{$ref} URLs are surfaced as \verb{*_ref} columns
rather than auto-dereferenced. Harvest athlete ids from
\code{\link[=espn_cfb_players]{espn_cfb_players()}}.

When \code{team_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN team catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_teams]{espn_cfb_teams()}}) is fetched once and friendly team fields are joined
in next to the \code{team_id} column -- \code{team_name}, \code{team_abbreviation},
\code{team_location}, \code{team_display_name}, \code{team_short_display_name},
\code{team_nickname}, \code{team_color}, \code{team_alternate_color},
\code{team_logo_href}, and \code{team_logo_dark_href}, inserted immediately after
\code{team_id}. A catalog failure degrades to \code{NA} rather than erroring the
wrapper. Set \code{team_detail = FALSE} to skip the catalog fetch and the
join.

When \code{position_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN position catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_positions]{espn_cfb_positions()}}) is fetched once and joined onto \code{position_id},
appending \code{position_display_name}, \code{position_leaf}, and
\code{position_parent_id} (the existing \code{position_name} /
\code{position_abbreviation} columns are left in place). A catalog failure
degrades to \code{NA} rather than erroring the wrapper. Set
\code{position_detail = FALSE} to skip the catalog fetch and the join.
}
